From d5d5d25764bed41e001c93a74bdfa7cf9e01c02f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: K0RE7 <>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Do not signal memory pressure for every new isolate

Worker::Isolate's constructor called
MemoryPressureNotification(kModerate) for every isolate. Since V8 14.7
(v8/v8@c407aa39d2), V8 handles any level above kNone by calling
WasmEngine::FlushLiftoffCode(), which drops the Liftoff code of every
wasm module in the process, and by releasing the isolate group's
memory pool. Every isolate then recompiles the wasm it runs.

The call has no other lasting effect: CheckMemoryPressure() resets the
level to kNone before the constructor returns, and the only GC action
for kModerate is to start incremental marking, which workerd disables.
---
 src/workerd/io/worker.c++ | 8 --------
 1 file changed, 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/workerd/io/worker.c++ b/src/workerd/io/worker.c++
index 6fb251b..9553176 100644
--- a/src/workerd/io/worker.c++
+++ b/src/workerd/io/worker.c++
@@ -1283,14 +1283,6 @@ Worker::Isolate::Isolate(kj::Own<Api> apiParam,
     jsg::isolateRegisterExternalReference(
         lock->v8Isolate, reinterpret_cast<intptr_t>(&messageCallback));
 
-    // By default, V8's memory pressure level is "none". This tells V8 that no one else on the
-    // machine is competing for memory so it might as well use all it wants and be lazy about GC.
-    //
-    // In our production environment, however, we can safely assume that there is always memory
-    // pressure, because every machine is handling thousands of tenants all the time. So we might
-    // as well just throw the switch to "moderate" right away.
-    lock->v8Isolate->MemoryPressureNotification(v8::MemoryPressureLevel::kModerate);
-
     // Register GC prologue and epilogue callbacks so that the current lock can release tracked
     // WebAssembly instances and count the full collections it pays for.
     lock->v8Isolate->AddGCPrologueCallback(
-- 
